    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d84">

                <pb facs="0132" n="122" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg122"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">127.62/6–2045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-20">June 20,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received June 20—8:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1016. General Wedemeyer and I issued the following joint statement to the press
                    yesterday.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Reports of dissension between ourselves or members of our staffs, either
                        personally or officially, are untrue. There have been differences of
                        opinion; however, they have always been resolved promptly and amicably. The
                        diplomatic and military representatives of the United States in China are
                        working together harmoniously and will continue to do so.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
